W: 1. All in a garden green
W: Two lovers sat at ease,
W: As they could scarce be seen among,
W: Among the leafy trees.
W: They long had loved y-fere,
W: And no longer than truly,
W: In that time of the year,
W: In that time of the year
W: Cometh 'twixt May and July.
W:
W: 2. Quoth he, "Most lovely maid,
W: My troth shall aye endure;
W: And be not thou afraid,
W: But rest thee still secure,
W: That I will love thee long
W: As life in me shall last;
W: Now I am strong and young,
W: Now I am strong and young,
W: And when my youth is past.
W:
W: 3. She listed to his song,
W: And heard it with a smile,
W: And, innocent as young,
W: She dreamed not of guile.
W: No guile he meant, I ween,
W: For he was true as steel,
W: As was thereafter seen
W: As was thereafter seen
W: When she made him her weal.
%
